# Grazing sea pass at the sub-solar point: the pivot sits 200 km inside the
# planet; the camera rides 1430 km from it at 16 deg of local azimuth, which
# puts the eye ~195 km above the sea looking ~15 deg below the horizon.
# Long water passes, max quadtree depth on shell and seabed, full atmosphere
# dome coverage. (For a subsolar pivot, key yaw = azimuth around the pivot:
# 0 = east, 90 = straight up; key pitch = elevation toward world +Y.)
view orbit
pivot subsolar
poff -200000
frames 480
simtime 0
key 0   1430000 16 0
key 480 1430000 40 0
